:29.718Z","effective_date":"2023-11-02","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-1319902-i20231102-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1205-a-2","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1319902-i20231102","date":"2023-11-02","original_code":"746.1205(a)(2)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-01-08","finding":"Responsibilities of Caregivers - Know number of children responsible for: Based on the information obtained during the DFPS investigation, there is sufficient evidence to support the claim that caregivers were not aware of the number of children they were responsible for and did not do a face-to-face name check during a transit period, which resulted in a child being left unsupervised on the playground.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026649499","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Caregivers - Know number of children responsible for (26 TAC §746.1205(a)(2))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1319902-i20231102-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1319902-i20231102","date":"2023-11-02","original_code":"746.1201(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-01-08","finding":"AP Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Ensure No Child Abused, Neglected, or Exploited: Based on the information obtained during the DFPS investigation, there is sufficient evidence to support the claim that abuse or neglect occurred when a 10 month old child was left unsupervised on the playground for 8 minutes.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026642651","violation_type_title":"AP Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Ensure No Child Abused, Neglected, or Exploited (26 TAC §746.1201(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1319902-i20231102-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1205-a-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1319902-i20231102","date":"2023-11-02","original_code":"746.1205(a)(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-01-08","finding":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity: Based on the information obtained during the DFPS investigation, a 10-month-old child was not properly supervised when they were left unattended on the playground for 8 minutes.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026654439","violation_type_title":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity (26 TAC §746.1205(a)(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1319902-i20231006","date":"2023-10-06","inspection_type":"Investigation of a report","result":"Deficiencies cited","passed":false,"violation_count":4,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905933725","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905933725","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2023-10-06","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[{"id":"tx-hhsc-1319902-i20231006-v1","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-2805-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1319902-i20231006","date":"2023-10-06","original_code":"746.2805(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-01-08","finding":"Prohibited Punishments - Corporal Punishment: Based on the information obtained during the DFPS investigation, corporal punishment was used when a caregiver forcefully removed a child from the carpet area, drugged the child to another part of the room to sit in time out, and then pulled the child by the foot when the child didn?t sit still.","topic":"facilities","source_record_id":"1026618444","violation_type_title":"Prohibited Punishments - Corporal Punishment (26 TAC §746.2805(1))","topic_label":"Facilities & equipment"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1319902-i20231006-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1205-a-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1319902-i20231006","date":"2023-10-06","original_code":"746.1205(a)(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-01-08","finding":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity: Based on the information obtained during the DFPS investigation, a caregiver was not properly supervising the children when the caregiver left the table where they were using a hot glue gun, accessible to the children, and went to the other side of the room to pick up toys. As a result of the glue gun being accessible to children, a child burned their lip on the glue gun.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026618446","violation_type_title":"Supervision ensures each child?s safety, well-being, including physical proximity and auditory or visual awareness of each child?s on going activity (26 TAC §746.1205(a)(4))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1319902-i20231006-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1319902-i20231006","date":"2023-10-06","original_code":"746.1201(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-01-08","finding":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control: Based on the information obtained during the DFPS investigation, a caregiver did not use good judgment by not seeking assistance when they needed help with children in the class, which resulted in a child being abused. Also, the caregiver did not use good judgment by leaving a hot glue gun accessible to the children, which resulted in a child being burned.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026618447","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control (26 TAC §746.1201(1))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1319902-i20231006-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1319902-i20231006","date":"2023-10-06","original_code":"746.1201(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-01-08","finding":"AP Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Ensure No Child Abused, Neglected, or Exploited: Based on the information obtained during the DFPS investigation, there is sufficient evidence to support the claim that abuse or neglect occurred when a caregiver forcefully grabbed a child and drug him across the room as well as leaving a hot glue gun accessible to a child which resulted in a child burning their lip.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026618445","violation_type_title":"AP Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Ensure No Child Abused, Neglected, or Exploited (26 TAC §746.1201(4))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1319902-i20230417","date":"2023-04-17","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905828651","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=905828651","retrieved_at":"2026-11-05T21:27:29.718Z","effective_date":"2023-04-17","evidence_class":"VERIFIED"},"occurrences":[]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1319902-i20230329","date":"2023-03-29","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905828650","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=90